# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "One group index per term is enforced {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"
msgstr "Um índice de grupo por termo é obrigatório {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The groups array holds one index per term, and assigning one of a different length raises. Nothing downstream re-checks the invariant, so it is enforced where the indices enter the operator: an array that is too short would silently drop trailing terms, and one that is too long would invent groups that no term carries.\n"
msgstr "O array de grupos contém um índice por termo, e atribuir um de comprimento diferente gera um erro. Nada no processamento posterior volta a verificar essa invariante, por isso ela é imposta onde os índices entram no operador: um array curto demais descartaria termos finais silenciosamente, e um longo demais inventaria grupos que nenhum termo possui.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clearing the group indices by assigning `None` is always allowed.\n"
msgstr "Limpar os índices de grupo atribuindo `None` é sempre permitido.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two checks are independent {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"
msgstr "As duas verificações são independentes {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") reports whether a group’s coefficients agree, which is the assumption [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") makes when it averages magnitudes. It is not a weaker form of the Hermiticity check: neither check implies the other, in either direction.\n"
msgstr "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") informa se os coeficientes de um grupo coincidem, que é a suposição que [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") faz ao calcular a média das magnitudes. Ela não é uma forma mais fraca da verificação de hermiticidade: nenhuma das verificações implica a outra, em nenhuma direção.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default the magnitudes are compared, because that is what [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") averages. A Hermitian conjugate pair with complex coefficients has equal magnitudes but unequal coefficients, so it satisfies only the default form.\n"
msgstr "Por padrão, as magnitudes são comparadas, porque é isso que [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") calcula a média. Um par conjugado hermitiano com coeficientes complexos tem magnitudes iguais, mas coeficientes diferentes, então satisfaz apenas a forma padrão.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") inherits the one-sided guarantee of [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): a `True` entry is always reliable, while a `False` entry is reliable only for operator types whose normal form is a genuine canonical form. Consult the specific operator type to find out which applies.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") herda a garantia unilateral de [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): uma entrada `True` é sempre confiável, enquanto uma entrada `False` só é confiável para tipos de operador cuja forma normal seja uma verdadeira forma canônica. Consulte o tipo de operador específico para saber qual caso se aplica.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

